<UserControl xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             x:Class="TanMenu.Wpf.Views.Settings.AboutCard">
  <!-- One settings row: 关于. See the "row spec's shared classes" block in
       Themes/Shell/Launcher.axaml for the anatomy, and AppearanceCard's code-behind for the full
       ReloadFromConfig contract every settings card group follows.

       WHERE THIS CARD LIVES — ROUND 8, TASK 4 MOVED IT, and not one line of markup below changed
       with it; this comment is the whole of that task's edit to this file. It
       is the whole content of Dialogs/AboutWindow.axaml, a modal About box the menu band's 关于 item
       opens. PUBLISHED, win-property-win: "Is the content solely an application's attributes? If so,
       use an About box." It is: this is the only settings group with no interactive control at all,
       which is the same fact that used to justify its position and now justifies its surface.
       (Round 5, item 2 — "关于集成到设置页中" — had folded it INTO the settings surface, as the last
       group of the 设置 page; Round 8, Task 2 turned that page into a tabbed dialog and this card
       became its sixth tab; Task 4 took the tab out. Its original placement argument pointed at
       Windows 11's own settings pages, which put identity at the end; Round 7 retired that reference
       with the rest of the Windows 11 shell, and no Windows 7 UX Guide page states an equivalent
       rule — recorded as provenance, not re-asserted.)

       WHAT IT REPLACED. 关于 used to be a rail row that raised a full-page overlay over 应用 — the
       startup splash card with its spinner swapped for a "点击任意处关闭" hint. The overlay was
       DELETED, not hidden, and this card is where its content went. Nothing else in the app shows the
       version or the copyright to the user except the startup splash's own footer, which is the same
       two strings from the same place (Services/AppIdentity.cs).

       THE ONLY VARIANT-6 ROW ANYWHERE: column 2 has no child. The Grid is the standard
       Auto,*,Auto anyway, because the header, the icon box and the expansion row are the same
       everywhere and an absent trailing control is not a different shape, just an empty column.

       ICON. The 16 DIP product tile rather than a Segoe glyph — this row is the app itself, and the
       image is already compiled into the assembly for SplashPanel and for the Aero caption's own icon
       (MainWindow.axaml's WindowDecorationsTheme). It
       carries tm-card-icon like every other row's mark; that class is :is(Control)-scoped precisely so a
       non-TextBlock leading mark needs no second rule. Height="16" is stated locally because the class
       deliberately sets Width only (a glyph's line box supplies its own height; an Image has none).

       THE TITLE IS A XAML LITERAL, and the one card title anywhere that is not localized: "TanMenu"
       is the product's name, identical in both languages, exactly as the overlay had it. The publisher line
       below it IS localized (AppLanguage's AboutPublisher) — the overlay's own "by TanSoft" was
       untranslated English, which is acceptable inside a branded splash card and is not acceptable as a
       settings-row subtitle.

       NEITHER VALUE LINE SETS A ToolTip, and that is deliberate rather than an omission. tm-card-value's
       rule in Launcher.axaml states that a value line whose text CAN outgrow the row it sits on and has
       no ToolTip is a defect in the card. Neither of these can: both are fixed formats over fixed
       content, not user data — and since Round 8, Task 4 the surface they sit on is a SizeToContent
       window, so the row is as wide as the widest of them BY CONSTRUCTION. (The measurements that
       argument used to rest on were taken at 150 % on the deleted 设置 page — 当前版本：0.12.0 at
       91.33 DIP of ink and the copyright line at 186.00, against a 599.33 DIP expansion row at the
       app's minimum window width. Kept as provenance, not re-asserted against a surface they were
       never measured on.) It is the same reasoning FoldersCard's DataInfoText records for going without
       one, and the opposite of its two path lines, which are user data and do set one. (An earlier
       revision of this note put the test against tm-card-value's own "260 DIP measure-time bound";
       that Setter was measured inert on a spanning expansion row and deleted — see the class's own
       remark.) -->
  <HeaderedContentControl Classes="tm-group-box" Theme="{StaticResource GroupBox}">
    <HeaderedContentControl.Header>
      <TextBlock x:Name="GroupHead" Classes="tm-group-head" />
    </HeaderedContentControl.Header>
    <StackPanel>

      <Border Classes="tm-card">
        <Grid ColumnDefinitions="Auto,*,Auto" RowDefinitions="Auto,Auto">
          <Image Grid.Column="0" Classes="tm-card-icon" Height="16"
                 Source="avares://TanMenu.Wpf/wwwroot/app-tile.png" />
          <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Classes="tm-card-text">
            <TextBlock Text="TanMenu" Classes="tm-card-title" />
            <TextBlock x:Name="PublisherText" Classes="tm-card-sub" />
          </StackPanel>
          <StackPanel Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                      Classes="tm-card-expander tm-card-values">
            <TextBlock x:Name="VersionLine" Classes="tm-card-sub tm-card-value" />
            <TextBlock x:Name="CopyrightLine" Classes="tm-card-sub tm-card-value" />
          </StackPanel>
        </Grid>
      </Border>
    </StackPanel>
  </HeaderedContentControl>
</UserControl>
